<div class="help-wrapper">
    <h1>Welcome to the WeConnect Dashboard!</h1>
    <h2>What is WeAre?</h2>
    <div class="items">
        <div class="item"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Afot8ypldsg">Origin of WeAre! Penn State</a></div>
        <div class="item"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D8591xRMIv8">Live of WeAre! Penn State</a></div>
    </div>





    <div class="ui segment">
        WeAre! is both a SlackBot and a community space for learners enrolled in PSU courses to engage with their peers
        and be part of the community. The WeAre! we propose here refers to a <a target='_blank'
            href="https://coil.psu.edu/blog/we-are-building-identity-participation-and-connectivity-within-world-campus-cohorts/">research
            project</a> aimed to connect
        learners across distance and build up their collective capacity as a community of learners. Thanks to the
        participation of numerous World Campus instructors and students, researchers from the College of Information
        Sciences and Technology at Penn State have found a lot about what a community of World Campus is for its
        members, using a mix of research methods, through a series of studies.
    </div>
    <h2>What is Slack team WeAre!</h2>
    <h3 class="ui header">What is Slack?</h3>
    <div class="ui segment">
        Slack is a team messaging application, with an expanded ecosystem of intelligent bots to help make your
        cooperation and collaborations with others easier. In slack, users can sign in to their workspace (in the form
        of domain.slack.com) in various manners (e.g. Desktop, Mobile Devices, or Web Browser). You can create or join
        any channels (public, denoted by #) or groups (private, denoted by 🔒). Please refer to the following links for
        getting started with Slack.
    </div>
