    <h3>How to use WeAre! bot?</h3>
    <div class="ui basic large  blue">There are three ways of using WeAre! in addition to the basic slack functions
        above.</div>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Onboarding/Self-intro <div class="subheader">/intro</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <img src="/images/intro-profile.gif">
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Once you join the team and consent to the research participation, you will be welcomed with a
                Slackbot WeAre! with the guide
                to introduce yourself (e.g. fun fact, city, profession). Then you will have the opportunity to be
                introduced by WeAre! to the team,
                and received a lot of love and support from your Penn State peers here.<br><br>
                In the future, whenever you want to get some support, you could always introduce yourself by /intro
                command in the text window and hit ENTER.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Study/Discuss with peers <div class="subheader">/we-discuss</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <img src="/images/we-discuss.gif">
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Initiating discussion with other channel members now or later. After typing the command, you can
                initiate a new conversation via Hangout/1:1 call or to schedule a meeting with other channel members.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Who is online with me now <div class="subheader">/we-are-now</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <img src="/images/peer-availability.gif">
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                See who is online now, and invite peers into a video session via Hangout call.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <h2> What is WeConnect Dashboard?</h2>
    <div class="ui segment">
        The WeConnect dashboard visualize the Slack activities and peer information to help you find other peers based
        on your educational interests, and organize social activities. For example, you might wonder
        who is available with you now to ask a question, and you can find that availability information in others'
        profile view. In addition, you can also go to the "Peer Availability" tab under the Connect in the Navigtation
        Bar.
        In the Availability view, you can easily see others peers' temporal availability based on their current online
        status, and their local time in different time zones.
    </div>
    <div class="ui basic blue large label">There are peers here visualized in the table view, or in the timezone
        distribution view. (More to come)</div>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Schedule and manage meetings
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                You can manage the meeting invitations by accepting or rejecting them. You can also create your own
                meeting by either going to the channel
                in which your meeting guests are in to schedule a meeting later (type in `we-discuss` and hit ENTER), or
                click the New Meeting button.
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <a href="/meetings"><img src="/images/meetings_screen.png"></a>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Browse your peers' educational information in the table view
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Who is in common with me in terms of major, location and channel subscription in Slack. Shared
                attributes are colored.
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <a href="/tablelist"><img src="/images/tablelist_screen.png"></a>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                View others' availability in terms of current presence and timezones
            </div>

            <div class="ui content">
                Who is online with me based on Slack logging status and time zone. Green dots show their online presence
                status. Click the image below or Go to the Navigation Bar and Select Connect => Peer Availability.
            </div>
            <div class="ui massive image center">
                <a href="/temporal"><img src="/images/temporal_screen.png"></a>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
